    "text": "In the circuit shown below, the key $\\mathrm{K}$ is closed at $\\mathrm{t}=0$. The current through the battery is\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/OL8UitofjZCK2t-T-_CHQZ8qxgA6RJc6s5gSK1w5aFg.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Z08e7",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{VR}_1 \\mathrm{R}_2}{\\sqrt{\\mathrm{R}_1^2+\\mathrm{R}_2^2}}$ at $\\mathrm{t}=0$ and $\\frac{\\mathrm{V}}{\\mathrm{R}_2}$ at $\\mathrm{t}=\\infty$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ll8uc",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{V}{R_2}$ at $t=0$ and $\\frac{V\\left(R_1+R_2\\right)}{R_1 R_2}$ at $t=\\infty$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "cat5E",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{V}{R_2}$ at $t=0$ and $\\frac{V R_1 R_2}{\\sqrt{R_1^2+R_2^2}}$ at $t=\\infty$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "80Qsc",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{V\\left(R_1+R_2\\right)}{R_1 R_2}$ at $t=0$ and $\\frac{V}{R_2}$ at $t=\\infty$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "At $\\mathrm{t}=0$, inductor behaves like an infinite resistance\nSo at $t=0, i=\\frac{V}{R_2}$ and at $t=\\infty$, inductor behaves like a conducting wire\n$$\n\\mathrm{i}=\\frac{\\mathrm{V}}{\\mathrm{R}_{\\text {eq }}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{V}\\left(\\mathrm{R}_1+\\mathrm{R}_2\\right)}{\\mathrm{R}_1 \\mathrm{R}_2}\n$$",
    "image": null
